-- title:
--   Smoothness defect drops under an affine dilatation
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain) with $\mathfrak m_R=(\pi)$, let $A$ be an $R$-algebra of finite type and $J\subseteq A$ an ideal containing the image of $\pi$, with $A/J$ endowed with an algebra structure over the residue field $k=$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField R` compatible with the $R$-structure. Assume the property: for $g\in A$, if for every discrete valuation ring $R''$ that is an $R$-algebra by a local homomorphism and satisfies `IsIndexOneExtension R R''` (namely $\mathfrak m_R R''=\mathfrak m_{R''}$ and $k\to$ `ResidueField R''` formally smooth) and every $R$-algebra map $c\colon A\to R''$ with $J\subseteq c^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{R''})$ one has $g\in c^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{R''})$, then $g\in J$. Let $R'$ be such an index-one extension of $R$ and $\varphi\colon A\to R'$ an $R$-algebra map whose generic point, the contraction of $(0)\subset R'$ along $\varphi$, lies in `Algebra.smoothLocus R A`. Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $A/J$ whose contraction to $A$ is $\varphi^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{R'})$, such that $A/J$ is smooth over $k$ at $\mathfrak q$ (`Algebra.IsSmoothAt`) and $\mathfrak q$ lies in `Module.freeLocus (A ⧸ J) ((A ⧸ J) ⊗[A] Ω[A⁄R])`. Let $A'=$ [`AffineDilatation.Ring J (algebraMap R A π)`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20), the $A$-subalgebra of `Localization.Away (algebraMap R A π)` generated by `gen J (algebraMap R A π)`, and let $\varphi'\colon A'\to R'$ be an $R$-algebra map restricting to $\varphi$ on $A$. Then, writing $\delta(f,a)$ for `smoothnessDefect`, the length over $R'$ of the torsion submodule of $R'\otimes_{\mathcal O}\Omega_{\mathcal O/R}$ for $\mathcal O$ the stalk at the image of the closed point, one has $$\delta\bigl(\operatorname{Spec}A'\to\operatorname{Spec}R,\ \operatorname{Spec}\varphi'\bigr)+1\ \le\ \max\bigl(1,\ \delta(\operatorname{Spec}A\to\operatorname{Spec}R,\ \operatorname{Spec}\varphi)\bigr)$$ in $\mathbb N_\infty$.
--
--   This is the affine-ring form of the decisive step of Néron's smoothening process: dilating a permissible centre strictly decreases Néron's defect of smoothness of an index-one point, i.e. $\delta(\varphi')\le\max\{0,\delta(\varphi)-1\}$. It is used by [`NeronModelInfra.exists_hom_isIso_smoothnessDefect_add_one_le_of_smooth_pullback_snd`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.exists_hom_isIso_smoothnessDefect_add_one_le_of_smooth_pullback_snd), which applies it on affine charts of the strata where the hypotheses of smoothness, freeness of the restricted differentials and the density property for $J$ hold.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NeronModelInfra_smoothnessDefect_affineDilatation_add_one_le_of_isSmoothAt_of_mem_freeLocus.lean

